{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:ClimaxVolumeMass.CoulombStrongRatioQRational","@type":"LeanModule","name":"ClimaxVolumeMass.CoulombStrongRatioQRational","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Exp"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.coulomb_strong_ratio_q_rational","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.coulomb_strong_ratio_q_rational","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/coulomb-strong-ratio-q-rational.lean#L70-L78","doc":"**Composite proposition** (`prop:coulomb-strong-ratio-q-rational`).\n\nThe Coulomb/strong ratio `tanh(ln q)` from `def:coulomb-charge`\nequals the q-rational `(q² − 1) / (q² + 1)` at every real `q > 0`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:coulomb-strong-ratio-q-rational","label":"prop:coulomb-strong-ratio-q-rational","md":"quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/coulomb-strong-ratio-q-rational.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.tanh_log_eq_qDiffOverSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.tanh_log_eq_qDiffOverSum","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/coulomb-strong-ratio-q-rational.lean#L46-L68","doc":"**Transcendental bridge** — Real `tanh ∘ log` equals the q-rational.\n\nFor any real `q > 0`,\n`Real.tanh (Real.log q) = (q - q⁻¹) / (q + q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.qDiffOverSum_eq_qSqDiff_over_qSqSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.qDiffOverSum_eq_qSqDiff_over_qSqSum","kind":"theorem","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/coulomb-strong-ratio-q-rational.lean#L28-L44","doc":"**Algebraic half** — pure-ring identity (no transcendentals).\n\nFor any real q with `q ≠ 0` and `q² + 1 ≠ 0`,\n`(q - q⁻¹) / (q + q⁻¹) = (q² - 1) / (q² + 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}